A||N||4||Verticalspeed||V8 Carb Hesitation On Acceleration...||||1||
Z||000000||Verticalspeed||12-28-2000||01:55 AM||||<B>SB 350 V8 carb question:</B><P>D:<BR>I have been experiencing minor but annoying <B>hesitation/surges</B> on acceleration...Runs fine during cruise and power mode.<P>Does this mean that the fuel pressure is too low? too high? Too lean, too rich? What typically causes hesitation? Fuel pump  is new. Holley pressure regulator set at 6psi with a <B>600 CFM eldelbrock.</B> Any edelbrock experts here? Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||12-28-2000||09:06 AM||||I am by no means a carb expert (this V8 Fiero is my first carb), but I do have the same carb as you.  I do have a slight hic-up when I go from idle to part throttle when its warm, but I'm using a very old carb.  I tried using different step up springs to no avail, and thought about replacing the accelerator pumps, but I've decided just to go with a new carb (the other reason is because it doesn't have a choke on it, and after all is said and done, its cheaper to just get a new carb with choke).  I've heard of several V8 Fieros running Edelbrock 600 carbs with no probelms, so I really don't think its a "all Edelbrocks in a V8 Fiero" problem.  <P>Time to start tinkering.....<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-28-2000||09:12 AM||||Check the accel pump on the carb. also check vacuum advance subsystem on the distributor. Either or both can cause this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||12-28-2000||11:29 AM||||How do the floats work on an Edelbrock carb?  I remember Holley's had center or side pivots, dpending on the model, and carbs were turned sideways on some 60's cars for some reason unknown to me.  Since most carbs are run in fore/aft setups, could having it sideways cause a problem with the floats moving (or not moving) on acceleration?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Verticalspeed||12-28-2000||12:36 PM||||Edelbrock tech pages suggest<P>a) Moving the accelerator pump link closer to the carb body for more fuel upon acceleration<P>Or<P>c) going one step richer in the cruise mode...<P>I have no problems once I am on the freeway or cruise speeds. It's definitely from a stop to getting going...flat spots and surges is what I am experiencing. Should I ruled out the spark plug wires since cruise-power modes are fine?||||reg||1
